 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "957f63cde2a2b80b6a3155a15a71a6f9a44b9558ecc0cc90896f8184b7336d1a"} {"question" "q-34361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ only"] ["text" "${b}_{1}$ only"] ["text" "${b}_{2}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only"] ["text" "${b}_{2}$ only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${b}_{2}$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-111091" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-111091" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}39 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}34 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-33 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, none of the vectors lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-111091" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "957f63cde2a2b80b6a3155a15a71a6f9a44b9558ecc0cc90896f8184b7336d1a"} {"question" "q-111091" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.j