\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -10 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-59 \\\\ 118 \\\\ -33\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -10 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 180\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, none of the vector lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34384" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "957f63cde2a2b80b6a3155a15a71a6f9a44b9558ecc0cc90896f8184b7336d1a"} {"question" "q-34384" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34384" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ only"] ["text" "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only"] ["text" "${b}_{1}$ only"] ["text" "${b}_{3}$ only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34384" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "None"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-111112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}28 & -7 & 14 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ k \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-111112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}28 & -7 & 14 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ k \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-7k+14 \\\\ k-2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-7k+14=0 \\\\ k-2=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-111112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "957f63cde2a2b80b6a3155a15a71a6f9a44b9558ecc0cc90896f8184b7336d1a"} {"question" "q-111112" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-111112" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-111112" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -15 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -15 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3k-15 \\\\ -2+k-3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3k-15=0 \\\\ k-5=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "957f63cde2a2b80b6a3155a15a71a6f9a44b9558ecc0cc90896f8184b7336d1a"} {"question" "q-34948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34947" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34947" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2k-8 \\\\ k+4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2k-8=0 \\\\ k+4=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=-4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34947" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "957f63cde2a2b80b6a3155a15a71a6f9a44b9558ecc0cc90896f8184b7336d1a"} {"question" "q-34947" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34947" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/questi