gned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2k \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4k-8 \\\\ 2k-4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4k-8=0 \\\\ 2k-4=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-74867" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "957f63cde2a2b80b6a3155a15a71a6f9a44b9558ecc0cc90896f8184b7336d1a"} {"question" "q-74867" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-74867" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-74867" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-74870" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 15\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-74870" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 0=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have two free variables, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}$  and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-74870" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "957f63cde2a2b80b6a3155a15a71a6f9a44b9558ecc0cc90896f8184b7336d1a"} {"question" "q-74870" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-74870" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{0}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-74870" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34334" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34334" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, and we have one free variables, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$\n\nFrom the second equation we get ${x}_{2}=4{x}_{3}.$ Substituting ${x}_{2}=4{x}_{3}$ into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(4{x}_{3})+3{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-11{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34334" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "957f63cde2a2b80b6a3155a15a71a6f9a44b9558ecc0cc90896f8184b7336d1a"} {"question" "q-34334" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34334" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{0}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}-11{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{3} \\\\ -11{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ -11{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34334" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{[\\begin{aligned}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -15 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -15 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -15 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 0=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have two free variables, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}$  and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "957f63cde2a2b80b6a3155a15a71a6f9a44b9558ecc0cc90896f8184b7336d1a"} {"question" "q-34951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{0}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have one free variable, ${x}_{2}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=-2{x}_{2},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "957f63cde2a2b80b6a3155a15a71a6f9a44b9558ecc0cc90896f8184b7336d1a"} {"question" "q-34333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{0}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-34333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-74872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 6 & -18 & 18 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-74872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 6 & -18 & 18 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -18 & 18 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, and we have one free variable, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$\n\nThe second equation tells us that ${x}_{2}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(0)+3{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-3{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-74872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "957f63cde2a2b80b6a3155a15a71a6f9a44b9558ecc0cc90896f8184b7336d1a"} {"question" "q-74872" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-74872" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{0}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "q-74872" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/state.json" "file_sha256" "d05b52825909934a0512cdab552abffb2799d70e561f1fb95b21200ec238a597"} {"question" "e-4810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix $A$ and vectors $\\mathbf{b}_1$, $\\mathbf{b}_2$, $\\mathbf{b}_3$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\textrm{Null}(A)?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/assets/9832b17728be69381a5f534317c0f30156fd32f3706f4cd4634765a02370180e.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/example-4810.json" "file_sha256" "5f8cec0dedabf33b13d287891684a711abcdbbf3dd0a63b77abe13dc24e2551c"} {"question" "e-4810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Null}(A)$ if $A\\mathbf{b}=\\mathbf{0}.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $\\mathbf{0}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-27 \\\\ 45 \\\\ 72\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\\,✓ \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 25 \\\\ 40\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $\\mathbf{b}_2$ lies in $\\textrm{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/example-4810.json" "file_sha256" "5f8cec0dedabf33b13d287891684a711abcdbbf3dd0a63b77abe13dc24e2551c"} {"question" "e-4812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/assets/a8b13d238a1e77d90abe70a505c68a72060ea95fe545f56ae53e7cf40ba0595e.png) and the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/assets/6e9f6c010c3137438923dfc32674dedf6d2d554b9b0a6745b007d826954d1e65.png) Find the value of $k$ such that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/example-4812.json" "file_sha256" "c7ab382faea39cd477f668c5b2e6bc8a2f390eb589c85ca2c5ced4ba7659a1fa"} {"question" "e-4812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Null}(A),$ then we must have $A\\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{0}.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ k \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6+2k-12 \\\\ -6+3k-3 \\\\ 12-6k+6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2k-6=0 \\\\ 